@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<article class="legal-page">
    <h1>TryOutSpot Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> May 2, 2026</p>

    <p>
        TryOutSpot is a baseball and softball tryout platform operated by Mid-America Services LLC.
        This Privacy Policy explains how TryOutSpot collects, uses, shares, and protects information
        when people create accounts, manage player or team profiles, register for opportunities, or
        receive account-related communications.
    </p>

    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>
        We may collect account information such as name, email address, phone number, password credentials,
        city, state, ZIP code, account type, and verification status. We may also collect player profile,
        parent or guardian relationship, team, organization, opportunity, registration, payment status,
        communication, and media information when those features are used.
    </p>
    <p>
        We collect technical information such as IP address, browser or device details, authentication
        events, security logs, and usage data needed to operate, secure, and improve the service.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>TryOutSpot uses information to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Create, verify, secure, and manage user accounts.</li>
        <li>Connect players, parents, coaches, teams, academies, and organizations.</li>
        <li>Support tryout discovery, registration, application management, and notifications.</li>
        <li>Send account, security, verification, password reset, and registration-related messages.</li>
        <li>Process payments, subscriptions, receipts, refunds, and related records when payment features are used.</li>
        <li>Prevent fraud, abuse, unauthorized access, and unsafe platform activity.</li>
        <li>Comply with legal, regulatory, tax, safety, and platform obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>SMS and Mobile Information</h2>
    <p>
        If you provide a mobile phone number and consent to SMS messaging, TryOutSpot may send transactional
        text messages such as phone verification codes, account security notices, password reset notifications,
        tryout registration updates, and other account or service-related alerts. Message frequency varies.
        Message and data rates may apply. You can reply STOP to opt out and HELP for help.
    </p>
    <p>
        No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional
        purposes. Text messaging originator opt-in data and consent will not be shared with any third parties
        except vendors that help deliver the messaging service, such as telecommunications providers, and only
        as needed to provide the requested SMS service.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Share Information</h2>
    <p>
        We may share information with service providers that help us operate TryOutSpot, including hosting,
        database, email, SMS, payment, analytics, security, and customer support providers. These providers
        may use information only to provide services to TryOutSpot.
    </p>
    <p>
        We may share information when required by law, to protect rights and safety, to investigate fraud or
        abuse, or in connection with a business transfer such as a merger, acquisition, financing, or sale of
        assets. We do not sell personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Children and Youth Sports</h2>
    <p>
        TryOutSpot is designed for youth sports participation and family management. Parents and guardians
        are expected to manage accounts and player profiles for children where required. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children under 13 without appropriate parent or guardian involvement
        and consent. If you believe a child provided information without appropriate consent, contact us so we
        can review and remove it where required.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Security and Retention</h2>
    <p>
        We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards to protect information.
        No system is perfectly secure, but we work to protect accounts, credentials, communications, and
        platform data from unauthorized access.
    </p>
    <p>
        We keep information for as long as needed to provide TryOutSpot, comply with legal obligations,
        resolve disputes, enforce agreements, maintain security, and preserve business records. Account
        deactivation or deletion requests may result in retention of limited records where necessary for
        legal, safety, payment, audit, or fraud-prevention purposes.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Choices</h2>
    <p>
        You may update account information, opt out of SMS by replying STOP, and unsubscribe from optional
        communications where available. Some transactional messages may still be required to provide security,
        account, payment, or registration services.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
        For privacy questions or requests, contact TryOutSpot at
        <a href="mailto:ewhitfield@midamserv.com">ewhitfield@midamserv.com</a>.
    </p>
</article>
